Respond with `Content-Type: text/event-stream`, `Cache-Control: no-cache`, `Connection: keep-alive`, and `X-Accel-Buffering: no` for nginx, then write `data: {json}

` frames as chunks arrive and flush after each, ending with a sentinel event such as `data: [DONE]`. Send a comment heartbeat (`: ping

`) every 15-30 seconds so idle-connection timeouts and proxies do not drop the stream. Include an incrementing `id:` so the browser's EventSource can resume with `Last-Event-ID` after a reconnect, and propagate client disconnect (request context cancellation) upstream to stop generating and stop billing. SSE is one-directional, text-only, and limited by per-domain connection limits on HTTP/1.1, so use HTTP/2 or a POST-based fetch stream when those bite.
